      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 140,
      "outputTokens": 1117,
      "costUsd": 0.010123,
      "pronunciationText": "When a rate of change is always the same multiple of the amount, we say the rate is proportional to the amount. Watch what that does. A lower point gets a gentler tangent, so the curve flattens as it falls. For a quantity Q changing over time t, the rule is d Q d t equals k Q. The number k is the constant of proportionality. For the car, k is minus point one five, and its unit is per year, because dollars per year divided by dollars leaves per year. If k is negative, a positive quantity shrinks, and more slowly as it gets smaller. If k is positive, it grows, and faster as it gets bigger."
    },
    {
