      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 169,
      "outputTokens": 1226,
      "costUsd": 0.0111185,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's a curve that fits. Q equals A, times e to the k t. Let's check it by substitution. From earlier, the derivative of e to the k t is k, times e to the k t. So d Q d t is A times k, e to the k t, which is k, times ay e to the k t. And A e to the k t is Q itself, so d Q d t equals k Q. That works for any A. At t equals zero, e to the zero is one, so Q is A. ay is the starting value. For the car, ay is thirty thousand and k is minus point one five. After eight years, it's worth thirty thousand e to the minus one point two, about nine thousand and thirty-six dollars."
    },
