      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 134,
      "outputTokens": 1009,
      "costUsd": 0.009148,
      "pronunciationText": "Often k isn't given, so we find it from data. A town had ten thousand people in twenty ten, and twelve thousand in twenty fifteen. Assuming the growth is proportional, when will it reach twenty thousand? Let t be the years after twenty ten, so ay is ten thousand. At t equals five, twelve thousand equals ten thousand e to the five k. Divide by ten thousand, so e to the five k is one point two. Take the natural log of both sides. Five k is the natural log of one point two, so k is the natural log of one point two, over five, about point zero three six five per year."
    },
