      "costUsd": 0.007170500000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Now set P to twenty thousand. Dividing by ten thousand gives e to the k t equals two. So k t is the natural log of two, and t is the natural log of two, over k. That's five times the natural log of two, over the natural log of one point two, about nineteen point zero years. So, if the growth stays proportional, the population reaches twenty thousand during twenty twenty-nine. Keep k exact until the end, so rounding doesn't creep in."
