      "pronunciationText": "Decay works the same way, with k negative. A substance has a half-life of twelve years. That means every twelve years, the amount halves. Start with two hundred grams. After twelve years there are a hundred grams, so a hundred equals two hundred e to the twelve k. That gives e to the twelve k equals a half, so twelve k is the natural log of a half, which is minus the natural log of two. So k is minus the natural log of two, over twelve, and that minus sign is the decay. After thirty years, Q is two hundred e to the thirty k, which is two hundred times two to the minus two and a half, about thirty-five point four grams."
